SECTION 1 (TCA 39-17-1307): Tennessee Code Annotated, Section 39-17-1307, is amended by deleting subsections (a), (e), and (g) and subdivision (h)(1)(B).
SECTION 2 (TCA 39-17-1307(f)(1)(A)): (A) Has been convicted of a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence, as defined in 18 U.S.C. § 921, within the prior five (5) years, and has not had the person's firearm rights restored pursuant to § 39-17-1367, or is still subject to the disabilities of such a conviction;
SECTION 4 (TCA 39-17-1307(h)(1)(A)): (A) Has been convicted of stalking, as prohibited by § 39-17-315, within the prior five (5) years;
SECTION 6 (TCA 39-17-1311): It is not an offense for a person authorized to carry a firearm pursuant to § 39-17- 1351 or § 39-17-1366 or a person who is not prohibited from carrying a firearm to do so in any state or local park, on a greenway or other recreational property, or, to the extent
SECTION 14 (TCA 39-17-1319(d)(1)(D)): (D) Hunting, trapping, fishing, camping, sport shooting, or other lawful sporting activity;
SECTION 17 (TCA 39-17-1321): (a) Notwithstanding whether a person has a permit issued pursuant to § 39-17- 1315 or § 39-17-1351 or § 39-17-1366, it is an offense to carry a firearm while under the influence of alcohol as defined in § 55-10-401(2) or any controlled substance or substance analogue.
SECTION 23 (new TCA 39-17-1367): (a) A person who has been convicted of a misdemeanor crime of domestic violence, as defined in 18 U.S.C. § 921, within the prior five (5) years may petition the court in which the person was convicted of the offense to have the person's firearm rights restored; provided, that the person may not petition the court until three (3) years from the date of conviction.
SECTION 23 (new TCA 39-17-1367(d)): (d) The court shall grant the petition for relief if it finds by a preponderance of the evidence and enters into the record the following: (1) The petitioner is no longer likely to act in a manner that is dangerous to public safety; and (2) Granting the relief would not be contrary to the public interest.
